1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,900
Onto the head of the
carpenter I was teasing,

4
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed at me for
still acting like a kid.

5
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I go chasing some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Pachinko in Kameari,
one yawn, and nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed-hat water basin,

9
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls toward the great heavens.

10
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this, too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika Shibamata,
losing happiness once again,

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,580
because I'm just a foolish
guy who tagged along.

13
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:31,340
An old man and a bomber

14
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,080
Well, you see, sir,

15
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,500
back when Abashin had his villa,

16
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:44,080
I was known as Okuyama,
the eight-man killer,

17
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,760
and people feared me, I'll have you know.

18
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,760
Now look at me, living in my undershirt,

19
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,640
That's a katsuagi

20
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,380
Hey, hey.

21
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,140
You there, young fella.

22
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:59,580
What is it, old man, you're still here?

23
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,520
You can go home now.

24
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:05,280
Hey, hey, with an interrogation like that,
the culprit won't crack.

25
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:07,220
What are you going on about?

26
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:09,800
Over a petty scam against a schoolkid?

27
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:13,240
Besides,
the other party withdrew their complaint.

28
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,160
With that kind of soft approach,
you won't get promoted.

29
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,700
How about we order some
katsudon and take our time?

30
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,600
Enough already.

31
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,440
I'm busy,
I don't have time for the likes of you.

32
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:30,700
Every single one of you.

33
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,640
I wonder if you can tell from this photo.

34
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:35,820
No way, no way.

35
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,660
A series of robberies.

36
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,580
Using a gun? How outrageous!

37
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,760
If you're going to use one,
you need to use your head more.

38
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,300
Hey, miss.

39
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:45,360
Hey there.

40
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,920
Hey, miss, sorry,
but could you get me a cup of tea?

41
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,700
I'm parched from questioning this rookie.

42
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:53,818
Haa...

43
00:02:53,868 --> 00:02:57,880
Has human kindness and
consideration run out entirely?

44
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,820
The Katsushika police weren't
like this in the old days.

45
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,160
The old Katsushika police weren't like this!

46
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:15,940
Back then, they treated even a gangster-type
city man like me with warmth and kindness.

47
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:20,380
Sometimes even young officers would
come to consult with a man like me.

48
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,660
They put on airs now,

49
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:27,400
but back when Gome-chan had just become a patrolman,
he had no money,

50
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:31,540
and women wouldn't look at him. He was known as Gome-chan,
the guy with nothing going for him.

51
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,840
Gome-chan?

52
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:38,080
Chief, this is an emergency!

53
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:44,120
Honestly, Gome-chan and the others were ridiculously,
hopelessly on track.

54
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,060
The moment they stood in front of a woman,
they'd freeze up.

55
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:49,760
They'd try to woo her,
sweat pouring off them like a waterfall.

56
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,340
The women all got scared off.

57
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:57,560
So, with no other choice,
I'd arrange their dates for them myself.

58
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,180
Okuyama-san.

59
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,360
Well, well, if it isn't Gome-chan!

60
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,200
And Dai-chan too, all of you together!

61
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:12,720
You know, there was that incident where
these two turned out to be total perverts.

62
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,980
Oh no, oh no, oh no.

63
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,980
Well then, I'll dig in!

64
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:21,320
Why should I have to pay for them?

65
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:25,200
Chief, last month's reprimand report.

66
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:25,620
Uh-oh!

67
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:27,920
Right when it was getting good.

68
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,240
I'm sorry.

69
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,540
I'll definitely write this month's too,
even if I have to pull an all-nighter.

70
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,580
You don't have to pay for that.

71
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,320
Instead,
I'm giving you a special assignment.

72
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,200
Uncle.

73
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:44,800
Well, I'd like some matcha ice
cream for dessert after the meal.

74
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,420
I've decided matcha ice cream
is what we have after a meal.

75
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,460
I won't eat anything but the Morikame,
that's the right one.

76
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,660
That place has the best one, after all.

77
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,360
Come on, Mr. Okuyama.

78
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,040
Sorry to interrupt your relaxation,

79
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:01,060
but Officer Ryotsu here will see you home.

80
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:01,920
Shall we go?

81
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,200
So it's you

82
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,100
Katsushika station's burden.

83
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,680
Disgrace to the police force.

84
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,120
Ryo-san from Katsushika station is

85
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:25,700
What did you say, you old geezer?

86
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,760
Out of the blue,

87
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:30,540
Ryo-san, I'm counting on you here.

88
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:31,260
Got it?

89
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:34,660
You understand?
Make sure you see him home safely.

90
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:36,220
Don't let your guard down.

91
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:37,680
Understood.

92
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:43,140
Damn, even if it's for
that incident report...

93
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,980
Why do I have to escort this old geezer?

94
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:52,340
What is it? Do you have something to say?

95
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:56,620
I just think you're a fine gentleman
with a truly distinguished face.

96
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:56,960
Understand?

97
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,080
There's no doubt about it.

98
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,880
I've watched police officers for years.
I can tell.

99
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:04,320
You're a burden to
Katsushika police right now,

100
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:07,200
but you have the face of a man who
will rise to become Japan's top cop.

101
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,340
R-really?

102
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,520
What do you think?

103
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,320
Let's get acquainted
over a drink at my place.

104
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,100
Nice.

105
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,660
When did you get that sake?

106
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,620
Where'd that come from?

107
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:17,180
F-from there? You mean...

108
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,660
Idiot, don't just take it without asking!

109
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,400
Geez, what an outrageous old geezer.

110
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,320
There, there.

111
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,880
This one looks better.

112
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:26,500
Hey.

113
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:27,480
Welcome!

114
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:32,240
No, hey, wait a sec, hold on, you!

115
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:32,840
It's the price.

116
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:38,040
Damn it, that old geezer, where'd he go?

117
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:41,462
How about it? It's a bit pricey, but

118
00:06:41,512 --> 00:06:42,760
it's a recommended item.

119
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:46,060
Just the right price.
My grandson will pay for it.

120
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,440
Hey, wait!

121
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,040
Kanao!

122
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:50,780
Kanao!

123
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:51,080
Kanao!

124
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:51,700
Kanao!

125
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:52,360
Kanao!

126
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:52,840
Kanao!

127
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,420
Kanao!

128
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:57,300
That man is Keiai, you know.

129
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,720
How could they make an elderly
man do something like this?

130
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:02,060
No, this is...

131
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:04,040
Yes, it's fine.

132
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,700
I'm just a useless good-for-nothing anyway,

133
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:08,177
just as you said,

134
00:07:08,227 --> 00:07:10,900
the old geezer gets sent
out barefoot in the cold sky.

135
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:13,780
Come on, hurry up and take me to Mage-yama.

136
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:16,540
W-wait, you idiot, don't say weird things.

137
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:19,760
You could at least buy him a pair of shoes,
you know.

138
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:22,520
Seriously, demons and devils are the worst

139
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:24,940
Isn't it pitiful for an elderly man?

140
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,200
That's right.

141
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:27,320
Exactly.

142
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:30,900
Hey, old man, how much is this?

143
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:33,780
Welcome back, thank you very much.

144
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:38,680
Sorry for making you go to all this trouble,
Ryo-san.

145
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:40,980
If you don't knock it off,

146
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,960
I won't go easy on you,
old man, even if you're elderly.

147
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,200
Where's your house?

148
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,640
It's right here.

149
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,280
What?

150
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,980
This is your father's house?

151
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:50,400
It's my son's house.

152
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,360
My son's...

153
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,860
That wife of mine left
the laundry out again!

154
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,220
Make yourself at home, don't hold back.

155
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,820
Whoa, that's amazing!

156
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:06,020
Napoleon and Hennessy.

157
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,260
It's all expensive liquor!

158
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,740
Go ahead and take whichever one you like.

159
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:12,160
Are you sure?

160
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:16,480
My son and his wife bring them
back from their overseas trips.

161
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,900
But living such a good life,

162
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,560
why would you go and
pull off some petty scam?

163
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:22,820
A good life?

164
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:28,640
My son is a top executive at a first-class company,
that's for sure.

165
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,880
My daughter-in-law is
a former Miss Universe.

166
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:34,040
My grandchild is the student council
president at a top-notch new school.

167
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,940
Even the cat has a pedigree award.

168
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,360
Go ahead and laugh, Ryo-san.

169
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:41,220
I used to swagger around
as a city councilman, but

170
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,660
you can't beat old age.

171
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:46,180
Now I'm living off my son like this.

172
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:47,180
But

173
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,440
after all, I'm just an ex-convict.

174
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:54,940
To my sons, I'm like a poisonous insect
that's latched onto their brand-new house.

175
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:55,540
Yeah.

176
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,200
My daughter-in-law says she
doesn't even want to eat with me.

177
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:00,480
And the grandchild...

178
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:03,820
Even now, my grandchild still calls me
"Grandpa."

179
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:19,960
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

180
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:21,980
That's the kind of old man I am.

181
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:24,600
Nooo!

182
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,600
You thief!

183
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:32,020
Wait! I'm not a thief!

184
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,120
Look! This is a warship!

185
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,140
Forgive the intrusion!

186
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:43,440
Breaking into the home of an eighth-dan
swordsman and fifth-dan marksman like me!

187
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:44,880
What nerve!

188
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:49,240
N-no! I-I brought your grandpa here!

189
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,320
There's no grandpa in this house!

190
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,920
What? He's your father too, isn't he!

191
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:55,740
Father?

192
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:01,380
He tricked us, that old geezer!

193
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:14,980
If I find you, I'll stick my hand in your
ear and rattle your back teeth, got it?

194
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,360
What do you want? You're coming, aren't you?

195
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,540
I quit.

196
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:24,080
What a lousy act you put on.

197
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:27,620
What do you mean,
the grandkids never once called me grandpa?

198
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,200
But Ryo-san,

199
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:33,240
I wanted to show off a little too, didn't I?

200
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,000
My real home is here.

201
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,520
Here? It's like a detective agency

202
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,840
Old man, don't you have any family?

203
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,860
It's just me.

204
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,920
They say
"home is wherever you settle," but that's a lie.

205
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,740
Even just to get through the rain here,
you need an umbrella.

206
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,480
Winters here are bitterly cold.

207
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:00,300
This is my own doing, I suppose.

208
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,920
Oh dear, I've run out of tea leaves again.

209
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:05,200
Water's fine for me.

210
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,600
Is that really okay?
I'll go buy some, so wait here a moment.

211
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,580
You've had a hard life too, old man.

212
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:17,440
What?

213
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,060
Not yet.

214
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,660
Finally, stop!
There's someone inside, you know!

215
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:46,740
!

216
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:48,120
Surely they've given up chasing us by now?

217
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,280
I thought he'd be a bit
more of a tough guy, though.

218
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:58,320
Could it be that you were
going to use me before...?

219
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:00,920
What?

220
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,560
That old geezer...

221
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:12,740
What's that?

222
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:36,939
The culprit fled into this department store around 6 p.m.,
pursued by police,

223
00:12:36,989 --> 00:12:38,220
ran all the way up to the rooftop,

224
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:41,860
and took an elderly man he
happened to run into hostage.

225
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:45,880
Suddenly, the man burst in, firing his gun.

226
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:50,460
I was desperate to escape. I was so
frantic I didn't know what was going on.

227
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:58,080
Whoa, don't shoot, you idiot!

228
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,820
Mirishou Kenbachon-kun was
the one doing the live report!

229
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,560
Hey! Help me!

230
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:06,080
Hey!

231
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:09,080
Damn it! The hostage is asking for help!

232
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,380
Hah! Whatever! I'm a cop!

233
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:14,460
Damn it! That old geezer again!

234
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,200
What? Isn't that Ryotsu?

235
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:17,660
Captain!

236
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:21,420
What happened to your face?
You've gotten even more handsome!

237
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:24,240
That doesn't matter! Let me in there!

238
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,400
No can do.

239
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:28,860
I've been ordered not to let anyone
in until the station chief arrives.

240
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:29,640
Station chief.

241
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:33,860
So, what are the culprit's demands?

242
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:38,120
They want five million yen
in cash and a getaway car.

243
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,260
Alright, I'll try to talk them down.

244
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,580
Do you think they'll go along with it?

245
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:46,540
Compared to old man Okuyama,
this is nothing.

246
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,120
Damn.

247
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,100
Hey, get away from here!

248
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,110
Damn it,

249
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:26,580
I have to bring that old geezer
back before the chiefs find out.

250
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:27,880
my position is at stake.

251
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,460
Attention, suspect!

252
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:36,540
I am Tonda Gomes,
chief of Katsushika Station!

253
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:39,120
Stop being foolish and come out quietly!

254
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:39,760
Shut up!

255
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,860
Leave the rest to you, Ohara.

256
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,620
Huh?

257
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:50,020
Geez, is that too much
for Gome-chan and Dai-chan?

258
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:53,620
Well, I've got no choice.
I'll have to protect myself.

259
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:58,040
Don't come near! Get five million
yen in cash and a car ready, quick!

260
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,400
Hah, how pathetic.

261
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,560
What?

262
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,580
The special forces will be storming in soon.

263
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,320
Poor thing,
you're going to be riddled with bullets.

264
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,000
N-no way, that's not true.

265
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,320
We've got hostages here, you know.

266
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:15,620
If you don't use your brains more, you
won't even escape what could've been escaped.

267
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:18,200
Don't underestimate the police of today.

268
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,100
What did you say?

269
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,960
Damn it, what are those guys doing?

270
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,750
Didn't I say so?

271
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,500
Holding out in a standoff is the hardest part,
you know.

272
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:33,400
All this time you've been spouting
nonsense like you know everything.

273
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:35,500
Who the hell are you, anyway?

274
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:39,450
Me? You know who I am, don't you?

275
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:42,660
The 1968 three-hundred-million-yen heist...

276
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:46,860
Of course I know that.
Don't tell me you're...

277
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,800
Well, fine. Go on, then.
Why don't you leave this to me?

278
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:52,720
What am I supposed to do?

279
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:54,920
The idiot's playing along,

280
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,820
first go to the emergency control room,

281
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:01,080
and make sure they can't get in.

282
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:11,720
What?

283
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,360
What's going on?

284
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:27,180
Chief, all entry routes into the
department store have been cut off.

285
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:27,580
What?

286
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,800
Ah test, test, test.

287
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:34,820
Station Chief Tonda Gomes, within one hour,
three hundred million yen in cash.

288
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:35,840
Five hundred million, I said.

289
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:39,080
Bring five hundred million yen in cash.

290
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,280
Get a helicopter ready for our getaway.

291
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,380
A jumbo jet to escape the country, got it?

292
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:46,220
And have a jumbo jet ready for
our escape out of the country too.

293
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,380
That old geezer...

294
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:50,940
Hey, are you okay, old man?

295
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:57,880
And bring Sushi Masa's nigiri!
Bring it to Tokujo-san!

296
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,860
Damn you, raising your demands like this!

297
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,080
I've never eaten Tokujo before.

298
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:05,220
Attention, suspect!

299
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,920
Your demands are completely unacceptable!

300
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:11,060
Release the hostage
immediately and come down!

301
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:12,940
W-what do we do, old man?

302
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,940
Just do what I say and it'll be fine.

303
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:17,690
W-that's...

304
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:21,100
This was back when current Station
Chief Tonda Gomes was still a patrolman.

305
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,660
Gomes, who fell for a
certain lady at first sight,

306
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:27,980
said he'd die if she wouldn't marry him,
and neglected his work entirely,

307
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:30,440
camped out in front of
her house for a whole week,

308
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,640
and nearly got himself fired.

309
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,180
W-what are you talking about?

310
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,460
Even that innocent young man grew older,

311
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:42,700
and now he has three mistresses.

312
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,100
What an enviable story.

313
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,740
Chief, is that true?

314
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,600
You idiot, that's complete nonsense!

315
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:52,640
But how does the culprit know such a truth?

316
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,160
It's not the truth.

317
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:58,160
Chief, could the elderly hostage be...

318
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:02,273
Damn it,

319
00:18:02,323 --> 00:18:06,760
isn't that like announcing that the
old man who never shuts up is here?

320
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:11,260
Now, next up, Honda, Komatsu,
Ohara, Daijiro, and Ryo-kun...

321
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:15,580
Like that time in Yoshiwara when we ran short
on money and it nearly became a police matter.

322
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,920
Chief, about that story...

323
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:23,420
Not good. Don't rush into making him the culprit.
Get ready so you don't regret it.

324
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,360
Initial response, G3.

325
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:32,720
First, I brought it to Tokuchou-san, sir.

326
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:41,980
Chief, what's next? Blow them up with a rocket,
hostages and all?

327
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:42,820
Chief!

328
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,400
Old man, you're amazing.

329
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,200
We split the 500 million yen, right?

330
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,060
Yeah, yeah.

331
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,400
Well, yeah.

332
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:51,392
Hey,

333
00:18:51,442 --> 00:18:55,640
Tell us about when you took the 300 million yen,
come on.

334
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:57,000
Mm.

335
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:01,520
Well, now.

336
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:05,500
Well, even I was nervous back then, I admit.

337
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,140
But I couldn't let this chance slip by.

338
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:09,340
That's what I figured.

339
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:12,480
So I went ahead and, on impulse,
gave it a try.

340
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:14,700
What the hell are you?

341
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,000
You old geezer!

342
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:19,520
I came in thinking you were dead,

343
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:20,720
and here you are,
stuffing your face with sushi!

344
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:23,320
Where the hell did you come in from?

345
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,180
Don't come near me!

346
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:25,880
Shut up!

347
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,080
I've got a bone to pick
with this old geezer.

348
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,280
You idiot!

349
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,700
I'm the one who has complaints here!

350
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:31,340
What?

351
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:34,080
Because of you,
my plan has been completely ruined.

352
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,680
It was probably some petty scheme anyway,
wasn't it?

353
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,320
Shut up and calm down!

354
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,420
That's enough out of you!

355
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:44,160
I've got no business with you!

356
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,760
W-wait, let's talk this through!

357
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:46,160
That's a lie!

358
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:49,680
I'm splitting the ransom with
the old man and skipping town!

359
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:51,540
I won't let anyone get in my way!

360
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:52,820
We split it fifty-fifty.

361
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:55,020
Well, you see, it just kind of happened.

362
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,480
Since you're in the way,
you're going to disappear.

363
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:01,820
Damn, I should've knocked him out
cold if I'd known this would happen!

364
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,900
You've really given us the runaround.

365
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,460
You bastard, what do you think you're doing?
If that had hit, what then?

366
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,980
It worked out, so we don't need it, right?

367
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:20,380
Shut up! The can of Sans just burst open right in front of my eyes,
didn't it?

368
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:23,340
Hey, what are you going to do now that
you've gone and gotten yourself like this?

369
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,860
How dare you betray me!

370
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:28,780
Look at this.

371
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:32,900
What, it's just a cow alarm clock?

372
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:34,760
This, this one.

373
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,980
It's a bomb, can't you tell just by looking?

374
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:41,000
I'll take you all down with me when I die.

375
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:41,820
W-wait!

376
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,180
Haaah!

377
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:47,020
Damn it.

378
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:50,500
It's a timer device,
so it won't explode right away.

379
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:51,800
Why?

380
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,080
You stupid son of a bitch!

381
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,860
Isn't there? I'm telling you, there isn't!

382
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,220
Hey, Jiji, retreat!

383
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,780
Ryo-san, just like that.

384
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:02,920
Go for it, go, go!

385
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:06,240
Leave it to me.
My knots were trained in the army.

386
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:08,140
Alright, this should do.

387
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:09,880
Well done.

388
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,180
See you.

389
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:12,860
Hey, where are you going?

390
00:21:12,860 --> 00:21:14,460
There'll be at least a cash reward,
you know.

391
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:19,340
Hey, the credit's all yours, Ryo-san.

392
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:23,160
Me, the one everyone
treated like a nuisance,

393
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:25,180
you put up with me so well.

394
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:27,580
Risking your own safety like this,

395
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:30,120
you came to help me, and I was so happy.

396
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,440
Yeah, yeah.

397
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:34,500
Take care, old man.

398
00:21:35,020 --> 00:21:38,240
Old man, if you get lonely,
come visit me to play.

399
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,540
You're a good guy, so be sure to come.

400
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,440
Aaaaaah!

401
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:50,200
What the... you actually did it, damn you!

402
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:54,360
There are still so many!
Ryo-san, hey! Come back here!

403
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:03,940
Looks like the suspect has been arrested,
reportedly by Yotsu.

404
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,560
Someone help me!

405
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:06,720
Hey!

406
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:11,000
The department store siege,
which was expected to be a long standoff,

407
00:22:11,020 --> 00:22:14,880
has amazingly ended with the suspect being
arrested by a single brave police officer.

408
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:19,100
Soccer Man!

409
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:22,920
What? The switch on the
dimension device is still on!

410
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:24,120
What!?

411
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:35,200
Ugh, there we go.

412
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,340
Is there no one here?

413
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,200
Reiko, Nakagawa!

414
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:45,300
Come on, Reiko-san.

415
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,100
Listen, I escaped.

416
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,540
You've already been
discharged from the hospital?

417
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:50,860
Oh my, Ryo-chan.

418
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:54,060
Senpai, are you really okay
to be moving around already?

419
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:57,040
Old man, what are you doing here?

420
00:22:57,480 --> 00:23:00,300
What do you mean? I took you up
on your offer and came to visit.

421
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:03,320
Ryo-san,
I hear you won the president's award.

422
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:04,480
Congratulations.

423
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,240
Thanks, you know.

424
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:09,200
Grandpa's really funny, you know.

425
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:12,600
Apparently he's an old friend of
the station chief and Chief Ohara too.

426
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:16,560
He's told us so many
interesting old stories.

427
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:18,740
Come on, Ryo-san, sit down, sit down.

428
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:21,320
This tofu is delicious.

429
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:23,580
It's handmade, the real thing.

430
00:23:24,020 --> 00:23:24,760
Alright!

431
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:25,707
Chief Ohara,

432
00:23:25,757 --> 00:23:29,000
what happened to the hot
sake I ordered earlier?

433
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:30,760
It'll be just a little longer.

434
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:31,800
Well, I'm off then.

435
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,660
Come here for a moment.

436
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,020
Ow ow!

437
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:37,260
Do you want to be hospitalized again?

438
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:40,120
Why is that old man Okuyama here?

439
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:42,160
How should I know?

440
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,400
In disguise.

441
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,880
Didn't you tell him to come?

442
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:47,380
I got beaten up.

443
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:54,620
Give me a break, please.

444
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:56,840
I'm a victim too, you know.

445
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:57,960
No way!

446
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:07,160
Honda, who keeps getting rejected,
has fallen in love again.

447
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,400
This time,
the target is a female Hakubai officer.

448
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:12,040
Alright, Honda,
hurry up and confess your love!

449
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:14,680
What? A strong rival?

450
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:15,820
Don't chicken out!

451
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:17,740
Go for it, even if you get shot down.

452
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:21,500
Next time, Honda's last love. Stay tuned!

453
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:37,280
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,

454
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:41,980
but I have so many things I want to do.

455
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride my motorbike
across the vast desert.

456
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,200
I want to be freer than a bird.

457
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

458
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,660
me

459
00:25:07,660 --> 00:25:09,900
me

460
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:11,680
me

461
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:14,160
me

462
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,400
me

463
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:25,040
me

464
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:26,100
me

465
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:27,100
me

466
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:28,360
me

467
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,600
me

468
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:41,880
Thank you for watching.

